From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: add the TVFE/TVCAP bring-up node

Without power on the TVFE and TVCAP domains every access to an HDMI-RX
window hangs the bus -- no abort, no watchdog. h713-tvcap (analyse/tvcap/,
a module rather than cstenger's builtin, so a failure costs a reboot instead
of a reflash) claims both domains and ungates the TV clocks, which is what
makes the INCAP window at 0x06940000 readable at all.

The node deliberately claims no interrupt: tvtop's GIC_SPI 110 (hwirq 142)
belongs to h713-afbd, proven on the device with 615 triggers. And no panel
properties: tvtop's panel_bl_en is PB5, which is the backlight AND the fan.

Origin: cstenger's EXPERIMENT patch 0087, on his board proven 02.09.2026.

This node was already live on our board, but only as a hand edit inside a
build tree -- it was never part of the series, so it disappeared the moment
a new tree was built (night 07.09.2026, package A: the whole INCAP block
read 0x00000000, TVCAP/TVFE showed "off" in pm_genpd_summary, and the
capture ring stayed empty -- a uniform green wall). Carrying it as a patch
is the fix; the series is the only thing that survives a rebuild.

Signed-off-by: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi	2026-09-06 22:09:53.442215090 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi	2026-09-06 22:09:53.449104951 +0200
@@ -1469,6 +1469,32 @@
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * TVFE/TVCAP-Inbetriebnahme. Ohne Strom auf diesen beiden Bereichen
+		 * haengt JEDER Zugriff auf ein HDMI-RX-Fenster den Bus -- ohne Abort,
+		 * ohne Watchdog. Beansprucht bewusst KEINEN Interrupt: tvtops
+		 * GIC_SPI 110 (hwirq 142) gehoert h713-afbd, am Geraet mit 615
+		 * Ausloesungen belegt. Und bewusst keine Panel-Eigenschaften:
+		 * tvtops panel_bl_en ist PB5, Hintergrundbeleuchtung UND Luefter.
+		 *
+		 * Herkunft: cstengers Patch 0087, bei ihm am 02.09.2026 belegt.
+		 * Der Treiber ist bei uns ein Modul, nicht builtin -- siehe
+		 * analyse/tvcap/h713-tvcap.c.
+		 */
+		tvcap_bringup: tvcap@50c0000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,h713-tvcap";
+			reg = <0x050c0000 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_TVCAP>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_BUS_CAP_300M>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_VINCAP_DMA>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_TVFE_1296M>;
+			clock-names = "bus_tvcap", "cap_300m", "vincap_dma",
+				      "tvfe_1296m";
+			power-domains = <&ppu 1>, <&ppu 2>;
+			power-domain-names = "tvfe", "tvcap";
+			status = "okay";
+		};
+
 		/* R-domain pinctrl for PL/PM banks (IR, S_PWM, WLAN/BT GPIOs) */
 		r_pio: pinctrl@7022000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-r-pinctrl";
